      "message": "Naming clash: the compiler already has an `own` flag on the libraries a loader serves (`library.own` in `lib.rs`, `Unit::own`), and there it means one of Vali\u0027s own libraries. Those may import `(vali primitive)` and link the `%` internal primitives. The lint origin here calls the user\u0027s code *own* and the standard library a dependency, which is close to the opposite set.\n\nIf the loader API grows a field for this, a host that sets the existing flag thinking it\u0027s the lint origin would give its libraries the internal primitives. A different word for the lint origin (*local*, *first-party* or *workspace*), in a separate field, would keep the two apart.",
